BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (purchases. Create a customer identifier, capture authority, attach a quote, calculate retained revenue, simulate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (collection, and reconcile the supplier statement. For a $10,000 customer invoice with $9,000 attributable supplier cost) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (under an applicable agency arrangement, the spread is $1,000, not $10,000 of scorecard revenue. At the matrix's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (domestic card planning rate, collection costs $290.30, leaving $709.70 before other operating costs; capped ACH) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (processing would cost $5 under the stated schedule, leaving $995. Actual authorization, settlement timing, return) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (exposure, and account pricing still determine the collection design. Do not extrapolate those illustrative contribution) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (figures into replacement annual scorecard margins. Then replay the same statement and webhook identifiers to prove) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (that no duplicate invoice, seat order, or commission is created. An operator should be able to trace every amount from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (signed terms through earning evidence to the bank entry without joining records by customer display name. Preserve) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (the dry-run artifacts as the template for first-deal review.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (Exercise the failures that can overwhelm a small team: an ACH return after provisioning, a duplicate supplier) Tj ET
